[[3,63,0,"<h3 class=\"step\" data-step=\"removing\" data-part=\"removal\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/20.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Removing</h3><a class=\"jump\" href=\"#\" data-jump=\"refitting\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/21.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Refitting</a><p><a href=\"#/2891951\">5550C30</a>\n                                           .</p><p>1. Rotate the bulb holder with the bulb in an anti-clockwise direction\nand extract it.</p><p>2. Extract the bulb from the bulb holder.</p><p>The bulb has a bayonet fitting.</p><figure class=\"photo\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2035452.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>"],[3,63,0,"<h3 class=\"step\" data-step=\"refitting\" data-part=\"refit\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/21.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Refitting</h3><a class=\"jump\" href=\"#\" data-jump=\"removing\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/20.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Removing</a><p>Fit the bulb in the bulb holder.</p><p>Insert the bulb holder with the bulb in\nits housing and rotate it in a clockwise direction.</p><p><a href=\"#/2891951\">5550C30</a>\n                                           .</p>"]]